  "nl_text": "The database schema named rschema_0375 consists of seven tables.\nThe Device table is used to store information about the devices in the network. It includes columns for Device_Status, ID (which is the primary key), IP_Address, Installation_Location, Installation_Time, Name, and Type.\nThe User table stores user-related information. It includes columns for ID (the primary key), User_Account, and User_Password.\nThe Staff table contains information about the staff members. It includes columns for Contact_Information, ID (the primary key), and Name.\nThe Network_Traffic table records network traffic data. It includes columns for Device_ID (which is a foreign key referencing the ID in the Device table), Download_Traffic, Timestamp, Total_Traffic, Traffic_Status, and Upload_Traffic.\nThe Device_Failure_Record table records device failure data. It includes columns for Device_ID (a foreign key referencing the ID in the Device table), Failure_Description, Failure_Occurrence_Time, Failure_Type, Handling_Status, and Remarks.\nThe User_Connection_Device table records user-device connection data. It includes columns for Connection_Time, Device_ID (a foreign key referencing the ID in the Device table), Disconnection_Time, Used_Bandwidth, User_ID (a foreign key referencing the ID in the User table), and User_IP.\nFinally, the Device_Maintenance_Record table records device maintenance data. It includes columns for Device_ID (a foreign key referencing the ID in the Device table), Maintenance_Content, Maintenance_Result, Maintenance_Time, Remarks, and Staff_ID (a foreign key referencing the ID in the Staff table).",
  "gold_question": "The wireless network monitoring and device management system primarily functions to manage device information, record network traffic data, track device failures and maintenance status, and monitor user connections to devices. The system is also capable of tracking maintenance operations performed by staff on the devices. The database includes the following functions:\n\nDevice Management: record basic information of all network devices. Fields include Device ID, Name, Type, IP Address, Installation Location, Installation Time, and Device Status. \n \nUser Management: store user account information. Fields include User ID, User Account, and User Password. \n \nNetwork traffic Management: record network traffic data of each device at specific time points. Fields include Device ID, Timestamp, Upload Traffic, Download Traffic, Total Traffic, and Traffic Status.  \n\nDevice failure record Management: record device failure information. Fields include Device ID, Failure Occurrence Time, Failure Type, Failure Description, Handling Status, and Remarks.  \n\nStaff Management: record information about staff members. Fields include Staff ID, Name, and Contact Information.  \n\nUser connection device Management: record the connection status between users and devices. Fields include User ID, Device ID, Connection Time, Disconnection Time, Bandwidth Used, and User IP.  \n\nDevice maintenance record Management: Used to document device maintenance information. Fields include Device ID, Staff ID, Maintenance Time, Maintenance Content, Maintenance Result, and Remarks.  \n\nThe design of thus system is primarily for device management, network traffic monitoring, failure diagnosis and handling, tracking user connection status, and maintaining device maintenance records.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_deepseek/0375.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0375\nCREATE TABLE `device` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `device_status` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `ip_address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `installation_location` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `installation_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_account` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `user_password` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `staff` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_information` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `network_traffic` (\n  `device_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `download_traffic` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `timestamp` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `total_traffic` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `traffic_status` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `upload_traffic` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  CONSTRAINT `network_traffic_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`device_id`) REFERENCES `device` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `device_failure_record` (\n  `device_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `failure_description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `failure_occurrence_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `failure_type` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `handling_status` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `remarks` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  CONSTRAINT `device_failure_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`device_id`) REFERENCES `device` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_connection_device` (\n  `connection_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `device_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `disconnection_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `used_bandwidth` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_ip` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_connection_device_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`device_id`) REFERENCES `device` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_connection_device_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `device_maintenance_record` (\n  `device_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `maintenance_content` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `maintenance_result` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `maintenance_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `remarks` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `staff_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  CONSTRAINT `device_maintenance_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`device_id`) REFERENCES `device` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `device_maintenance_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`staff_id`) REFERENCES `staff` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
